# Admin Auto-Promote via Environment Variable

## Summary

Add `ADMIN_EMAIL` environment variable. When a user signs up with that email, they automatically get `role = "admin"`.

---

## Implementation

### Modify `backend/internal/handlers/auth.go`

In the `Signup` function, after creating the user struct but before saving:

```go
// Check if this email should be auto-promoted to admin
adminEmail := os.Getenv("ADMIN_EMAIL")
role := "user"
if adminEmail != "" && strings.EqualFold(req.Email, adminEmail) {
    role = "admin"
}

user := models.User{
    Email:           req.Email,
    Name:            req.Name,
    PasswordHash:    hashedPassword,
    Role:            role,  // was hardcoded "user"
    // ... rest unchanged
}
```

**Location:** Around line 159-167 in auth.go

---

## Usage

### Local Docker Testing
In `docker-compose.yml`, add to backend environment:
```yaml
environment:
  ADMIN_EMAIL: your@email.com
```

### AWS Production
Set environment variable in your ECS task definition / EC2 / etc:
```
ADMIN_EMAIL=your@email.com
```

---

## Security Notes

- Only works on **signup**, not login (can't promote existing users)
- Case-insensitive email comparison
- Once you're admin, you can use the invitation system to invite others
- Consider removing the env var after initial setup (optional)

